0	section	Speaking to the Watchtower Wizard
1	line	Watchtower Wizard	Who are you? Are you one of the new guards?
1	line	Player	No, I'm an adventurer.
1	line	Watchtower Wizard	Well what are you doing here?
1	line	Player	Looking for adventures - what else?
1	line	Watchtower Wizard	Oh my, oh my! What does it all matter in the end, anyway?
1	select	Select an Option
1	option	What's the matter?
2	line	Player	What's the matter?
2	line	Watchtower Wizard	Oh dear, oh dear. Darn and drat!
2	line	Watchtower Wizard	We try hard to keep this town protected.
2	line	Watchtower Wizard	But how can we do that when the Watchtower isn't working?
3	line	Player	What do you mean it isn't working?
2	line	Watchtower Wizard	The Watchtower here works by the power of magic. An ancient spell designed to ward off ogres that has been in place here for many moons.
2	line	Watchtower Wizard	The exact knowledge of the spell is lost to us now, but the essence of the spell has been infused into four powering crystals that keep the tower protected from the hordes in the Feldips.
2	select	Select an Option
2	option	So how come the spell doesn't work?
3	line	Player	So how come the spell doesn't work?
3	line	Watchtower Wizard	The crystals! The crystals have been taken!
3	line	Player	Taken?
3	line	Watchtower Wizard	Stolen!
3	line	Player	Stolen?
3	line	Watchtower Wizard	Yes, yes! Do I have to repeat myself?
3	select	Start the Watchtower quest?
3	option	Yes.
4	line	Player	Can I be of help?
4	line	Watchtower Wizard	Help? Oh wonderful, dear traveller!
4	line	Watchtower Wizard	Yes I could do with an extra pair of eyes here.
4	line	Player	???
4	line	Watchtower Wizard	There must be some evidence of what has happened here. Perhaps you could assist me in searching for clues?
4	line	Player	I would be happy to.
4	line	Watchtower Wizard	Try searching the surrounding area. If you find anything unusual, bring it here. Try the bushes - I've read enough adventure stories to know that clues get caught in bushes all the time.
4	line	Watchtower Wizard	I will tell the guards to let you past - that way, you can just use the ladder to get in and out.
4	action	end
3	option	No.
4	line	Player	I'm not interested.
4	line	Watchtower Wizard	That's typical, nowadays. It's left to us wizards to do all the work.
4	action	end
2	option	I'm not interested in your rantings.
3	line	Player	I'm not interested in your rantings.
3	line	Watchtower Wizard	Hmph! Suit yourself.
3	action	end
1	option	You wizards are always complaining.
2	line	Player	You wizards are always complaining.
2	line	Watchtower Wizard	Complaining? Complaining!
2	line	Watchtower Wizard	What folks these days don't realise is that if it weren't for us wizards, this entire world would be overrun with every creature you could possibly imagine. And some you couldn't even conceive of!
2	action	end
